# MAINBASE — `claude/av1-unified` rebuilt on `main`

Row 150 of [`queue.md`](queue.md) (on `claude/av1`). `claude/av1-unified` was cut from `main` at `8407095` (PR #33),
before `main` took PR #34, the server refactor (`c7230a9`, 48 files); a trial merge stopped on 24 of them. The branch
is now rebuilt on `c7230a9`: the final PR to `main` is a fast-forward, and every file PR #34 touched is listed below
as `main` has it or with each change the branch makes to it.

**What was done, 2026-10-12.**

* Every commit of `claude/av1-unified` and `claude/av1` not on `main` — 1 557 commits — was written again with author and
  committer `dary-dc <crespoydelgado@gmail.com>`, dates, messages and parents kept but for the replacements below.
  Signatures (`gpgsig`) could not survive a new hash and were dropped.
* The 423 commits that descend from `8407095` (the branch's own line since it was cut) were replayed onto
  `c7230a9`: each one's tree is its old tree merged with PR #34 (`git merge-tree`, base `8407095`), its conflicts
  resolved as §The conflicts says. The rest — `claude/av1`'s line, which forked from `main` at `495ccd6`
  before PR #33 and is merged into this branch again and again — kept their trees: they do not descend from
  `8407095`, so PR #34 has nothing to replay onto them, and the merges that bring them here are replayed like any
  other commit.
* **Every hash reference follows.** Each 7–40-hex token in a tree or a message that named exactly one replaced commit
  now names its replacement, at the same length unless that prefix is ambiguous (92 287 tokens over the history).
  The map is `docs/av1/rehash-map.tsv` on `claude/av1`, and `docs/av1/rehash_check.py` there prints every token left
  naming a replaced commit. One file is left as it is on purpose: `docs/cloud-queue.md` belongs to another queue and
  is never edited here, so its two tokens naming replaced commits stay as they are; the map gives their replacements.
* The old tips stay reachable as `claude/av1-unified-pre-main` and `claude/av1-pre-main` until the owner has looked.

## Verification

**(a) Outside PR #34's files, the old tip and the new differ by hash replacements alone.** Of the paths
outside PR #34's 48 (under the branch's names for the ones it moved), 20 differ between `claude/av1-unified-pre-main` and the replayed
tip `7cb02d3f`, and every one of them is equal once each token naming a replaced commit is written as its
replacement; none is added, removed or otherwise changed. (`docs/av1/rehash_verify.py` on `claude/av1` makes that reading.)

**(b)** This file: §PR #34's files and §The conflicts.

**(c) The full gate is green on the new tip** (`scripts/gate.sh`, `GATE OK in 236 s`; skipped by name, as on any host without numpy, pydicom or a GL display: the DICOM reader's tests, the painter check, the split's merge test, and the viewer's cross-codec arm and Firefox), the decoder builds made with
`client/decode/wasm/build/build.sh` and checked against their manifest, so the viewer's page check ran:
every frame complete, exact and drawn in headless Chromium (3/3 exact, HTJ2K), and the real-server checks over QUIC and the WebSocket in Chromium. Firefox was not run: the viewer's Firefox arm needs a GL display this container lacks. The old tip failed the same gate at its link check (`docs/ingest/README.md` linked a `contract.md` not yet
written); the new tip's last commit names it unlinked.

**(d) The final PR** (`main...claude/av1-unified`, 1 335 files, +77 274 −5 444, a fast-forward of `main`), by area:

* **The AV1 path** — `lab/av1/` (314 files, the phase's measurements and fixtures), `client/contract/av1/` and
  `client/contract/` (489 files: golden payloads and the contract suite renamed from `client/conformance/`),
  `client/decode/` (the decoder builds and workers), `client/paint/` and `client/viewer/` (the painter and the
  viewer page), `ingest/coded-frames/` and `ingest/from-dicom/`.
* **The server** — `server/src/` (18 files, +973 −279: the BBR loss bound, the controller trace, row 54's tests
  and the renames, on PR #34's structure), `common/` (`study-bundle` moved to `common/series-bundle/`, the
  envelope's `INDEX_LEN`), `server/scripts/`.
* **The lab** — `lab/decode-bench/`, `lab/bb3/`, `lab/recv-cost/`, `lab/page-open/`, `lab/disk-access-bench/`
  and some 40 more folders; `lab/scripts/` renamed by what each script measures.
* **Docs** — `docs/av1/` (the phase, its queue's reports), `docs/adr/`, `docs/transport/`, `docs/decode/`,
  `docs/codecs/`, `docs/native/`, `docs/ingest/`, the glossary; `README.md` and `CLAUDE.md`.
* **Repository** — `scripts/` (the gate and its checks), `deploy/`, `.gitignore`, `.nvmrc`, `Cargo.toml` and
  `Cargo.lock`, the renamed wtransport patch under `patches/`.

## What the branch adds on top of the replay

Two commits after the replayed tip, both small:

* `ce3f1fa0` — PR #34's own code and docs in the branch's names, where they merged cleanly but named what the branch
  renamed: `fill_load.rs` takes `MAX_FRAME_LEN` from `frame-envelope` (PR #34 moved it there from the harness's
  `wire.rs`), PR #34's new tests and comments in `frame_store.rs` and `format.rs` say *series*, `FIXTURES.md` says
  `pack-series`, `server/README.md` (PR #34's map) names `FillReader`, `Command` and the series bundle, and
  `server-design-proposal.md` names the four moved paths where they are now.
* `d1e7aa15` — `docs/ingest/README.md` names `contract.md` as not yet written instead of linking it, so the gate's
  link check passes (it failed on the old tip too).

## The conflicts

The 24 files that stopped the trial merge, as resolved on the tip. Each keeps PR #34's structure and re-applies the
branch's change on top of it. The branch's changes in them are almost all row 84's renames
(`f5066336`, `0c416d79`, `6057a35e`: *study* → *series*, `exact-server` → `series-server`, `SeqReader` →
`FillReader`, the planner's `Ask` → `Command`, `ENVELOPE_LEN` → `INDEX_LEN`, `parse_open_ask` →
`parse_opening_ask`, a lab *arm* → *variant*), plus row 54's tests (`f4159400`) and the BBR loss bound
(`loss_bound.rs`, `cc_trace.rs`).

| File | PR #34 | The branch | Resolved |
| --- | --- | --- | --- |
| `Cargo.lock` | `study-bundle` depends on `frame-envelope` | the crate is `series-bundle` | regenerated by `cargo`: `series-bundle` with the dependency |
| `client/transport/wasm/src/session.rs` | the length check is `frame_envelope::envelope_len` | `ENVELOPE_LEN` → `INDEX_LEN` in the inline check | PR #34's call; the constant's new name lives in the crate |
| `common/frame-envelope/src/lib.rs` | `MAX_FRAME_LEN`, `MAX_CODESTREAM_LEN`, `envelope_len` | `ENVELOPE_LEN` → `INDEX_LEN` | PR #34's additions, with `INDEX_LEN`, its test too |
| `common/series-bundle/src/writer.rs` | a test: an oversized frame is refused | a test: a frame the index did not declare is refused | both tests; PR #34's says *series* |
| `docs/WIRE.md` | an opening ask is never refused (corrected in place); a series over the limit fails to open | *arms the fill* → *variants the fill*; *study* → *series* | PR #34's text, the anchor to `#sbnd-series-bundle`; *arms the fill* kept, since row 84's rename keeps arming's verb |
| `docs/adr/client-window-depth.md` | `frame_out.rs` → `link.rs` | *arm* → *variant* | both |
| `docs/adr/disk-access.md` | `Next::Fill`'s `after`, `link.rs`, *a fill's one ahead* | `FillReader`, *variant* | both, and PR #34's *the study's `FrameStore`* says *series* |
| `docs/adr/frame-framing-and-loop-shape.md` | `Next::Fill`'s `after` | `FillReader` | both |
| `docs/adr/telemetry-server-pipeline.md` | the refusal paragraph rewritten for row v3; "both arms record" | *study* → *series* in the old paragraph | PR #34's paragraph; *both variants record* |
| `ingest/study-bundle/Cargo.toml` | depends on `frame-envelope` | moved to `common/series-bundle/` | the dependency added there (`../frame-envelope`) |
| `lab/disk-access-bench/src/bin/read_campaign.rs` | `SeqReader::new(store)` | `FillReader` | `FillReader::new(Arc::clone(&store))` |
| `lab/disk-access-bench/src/main.rs` | `frame_span` cannot fail (no `?`) | `StudyMap` → `SeriesMap`, `Arm` → `Variant` | both |
| `lab/scripts/telemetry_e2e_baseline.sh` | `DEFAULT_TELEMETRY=1`; the dropped harness flag | `series-server`, `--variant` | both |
| `server/scripts/check_telemetry_absent.sh` | the field names dropped from the symbol list | `series_server`, two fields dropped | PR #34's list under `series_server` |
| `server/src/main.rs` | `TransportTuning` flattened into `Args` | `series_server`; `bbr-bound` parsed in a test; *series* | PR #34's `Args`; the branch's `bbr-bound` test through `.tuning` |
| `server/src/media/read_path.rs` | the fill reader owns its store | `FillReader`, a shorter doc comment | PR #34's code under `FillReader`, the shorter comment |
| `server/src/record/tap.rs` | `t_ask_us` and `prepare_us` gone (row v3) | `prepare_us`'s comment trimmed | PR #34's: the field is gone |
| `server/src/transport/frame_out.rs` | moved into `link.rs` | `within` and `take_priority` taken out, with two tests (`f4159400`) | applied to `link.rs`: the stall's cut through `within`, `Media::send` through `take_priority`, both tests |
| `server/src/transport/mod.rs` | `link` for `frame_out` | `cc_trace`, `loss_bound` | all three |
| `server/src/transport/pipeline.rs` | read then write through `Link`; the late-control test moved to `link.rs` | `FillReader`, `INDEX_LEN`, *series* | PR #34's code under the branch's names |
| `server/src/transport/planner.rs` | the planner checks every range; `Next`, `Fill` | `Command`; `f4159400` drops the `end_stream` pop after a cut fill, holds the flood test to `<`, adds a look-ahead test | PR #34's planner under `Command`, the pop dropped (its loop takes an `EndStream` with `continue`), the new test against `Step::Serve { next }`, "series is empty" |
| `server/src/transport/server.rs` | `parse_open_ask` checks ranges; `ControlFlow` | `Command` | PR #34's code under `Command` |
| `server/src/transport/tuning.rs` | the knobs are `clap` arguments with help text | quinn's default numbers out of the comments | PR #34's `#[arg]`s, the numbers out |
| `server/src/transport/websocket.rs` | `Link` | `parse_opening_ask` | both |

**The history before the tip.** 55 distinct conflicts arise over the replayed commits (a file at one
version of the branch against PR #34). The tip's 24 are above. Of the rest, 25 are hunks where the branch only
renamed words: PR #34's side with the same renames, as the branch stood at that commit. 3 (`tuning.rs` twice,
`writer.rs` before its move) carry the branch's change from that version to the tip's onto the tip's resolution, a
three-way merge with no conflict. 3 were resolved by hand in the tip's way: `planner.rs` twice (the pop
dropped, the flood comment, the look-ahead test against `Step::Serve { next }`) and `mod.rs` once (`link` and
`loss_bound`, before `cc_trace`). Commits between are not built one by one; the gate runs on the tip.

